SEALED 2026-08-19, run #4 cycle 5, BEFORE any fixer agent was dispatched.

The gate file itself is held at SWARM/runs/run4-cycle-005-gate.mjs for the whole dispatch
window. Hard rule 5 gives workflow agents TARGET paths only and never SWARM paths, so the
check is STRUCTURALLY unreachable to a fixer rather than merely forbidden to it (the run #3
cycle-14 decision). Only this hash and the baseline below live in the target during dispatch.

DISCRIMINATING PRE-DISPATCH BASELINE — 16 PASS / 4 FAIL on the UNFIXED tree.
Full output: run4-cycle-005-baseline-gate.txt

The four FAILs are exactly the scope of the two reproduced findings, and nothing else:
  R1  README asserts an unqualified "most recent full matrix"
  R5  that recency claim is false against the live API (newest is 32274489339, not the cited 32267338333)
  P1  REPORT still carries the false wrapper "twice in this cycle alone"
  P4  that sentence scopes both examples to one cycle and never names cycle 4

Everything a correct fix must NOT disturb already passes and must still pass afterwards:
R2 (citation not deleted), R3 (four-version table intact), R4 (cited run really is a green
4-job matrix), R6 (verified-at-18 honesty wording), P2 (both historical examples survive),
P3 (the running total of eight survives — B-1b was REFUTED, so eight is true and deleting
it would remove a true claim), P5 (dated snapshot framing), G1/G2 (suite 118/118/0 with a
parser proven to read a red run as red), G3 (the two out-of-scope files byte-unchanged),
G4 (src/ bin/ test/ untouched, still zero-dependency), G5 (only README.md and REPORT.md move).

TWO GATE BUGS WERE FOUND BY THIS BASELINE AND REPAIRED BEFORE SEALING.
Fixing before a gate has run is repair; editing after it has run destroys the evidence of
what it measured.

1. UNBOUNDED RECURSION. Cells were evaluated eagerly at registration, so the control cells
   C1-C4 — which re-invoke this same file with --only — ran the controls inside every
   control. The first baseline never terminated. Cells are now registered and evaluated
   only after --only is parsed, so a --only run evaluates exactly one cell.

2. A MATCHER BLIND TO LINE-WRAPPING. Both documents are hard-wrapped markdown, so the
   claim under review is physically stored as "including twice\nin this cycle alone".
   The phrase cells matched the raw text and could not see through the break. The
   consequence is the important part: P1 reported the false sentence ABSENT on a tree that
   contains it — a cell that fails OPEN — while P2 reported an intact example as DELETED.
   One root cause, opposite directions. Phrase cells now match whitespace-normalised text;
   only line-oriented cells use the raw text.

Two bugs in twenty cells is the standing argument for baselining a gate rather than
reasoning about it. Bug 2 in particular would have certified the REPORT.md defect as fixed
without any fix at all.
